An analysis was conducted on the decays $B^{+} 	o D^{+} \ell^{+} 
u_{\ell}$ and $B^{+} 	o D^{+} \ell^{-} 
u_{\ell}$, where $\ell$ represents either an electron or muon. This analysis utilized a dataset consisting of 3.0 fb$^{-1}$ of and was obtained from the LHCb experiment, where the data was collected at a center-of-mass energy of 7 TeV in 2011. The obtained results for the branching fractions were used to set a 95% confidence level upper limit for the decay $B^{+} 	o D^{+} \gamma$, and semileptonic decays $B^{+} 	o D^{+} \ell^{-} 
u_{\ell}$ were found to be in line with the Standard Model predictions.
